-2026.html#thm:main","release_id":"openai-math","schema":"statement-map-web/2","section":1,"section_title":"Introduction","source":{"current_hash_method":"tex-environment-body-comments-removed","current_statement_sha256":"sha256:356002a2c0aefc59e9b5b652b9af817c2959ff08d8c6d02460156b0760bbaf8e","file":"preprints/Witnessed-symmetric-choice-is-strictly-stronger-than-choiceless-polynomial-time-with-counting-September-24-2026/build/sections/00-introduction.tex","line":38,"producer_hash_method":"atlas-whitespace-normalized-text","producer_statement_sha256":"cbc289e3bfae0a29657a8a644e93e0121cbef52703924051bd3ba1e6c1114853","provenance":{"kind":"computed","pin":"fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb","source":"preprints/Witnessed-symmetric-choice-is-strictly-stronger-than-choiceless-polynomial-time-with-counting-September-24-2026/build/sections/00-introduction.tex"},"sha256":"sha256:356002a2c0aefc59e9b5b652b9af817c2959ff08d8c6d02460156b0760bbaf8e","url":"https://github.com/openai/math/blob/fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb/preprints/Witnessed-symmetric-choice-is-strictly-stronger-than-choiceless-polynomial-time-with-counting-September-24-2026/build/sections/00-introduction.tex#L38"},"statement_kind":"theorem","text":"\\label{thm:main}\nThere exist a vocabulary \\(\\tau\\) of eight binary relations, a fixed polynomial\n\\(p\\), and a \\(\\CPT+\\WSC\\) sentence \\((\\Phi,p)\\) with one occurrence of a WSC\noperator such that:\n\\begin{enumerate}[label=\\textup{(\\roman*)}]\n\\item \\((\\Phi,p)\\) has a Boolean value on every finite \\(\\tau\\)-structure;\n\\item no \\(\\CPT\\) sentence over \\(\\tau\\) has the same true-model class.\n\\end{enumerate}\nThe \\(\\CPT\\) sentences in \\textup{(ii)} may use counting and hereditarily\nfinite sets of unrestricted finite rank."}
